      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense that denial of improvement feels so painful when your reality is fundamentally hollow without him; that depth of loss often outlasts the initial phases of grief. While rebuilding hasn't seemed possible yet, many people eventually find a quiet moment where the absence creates space for new experiences to finally make sense. Please reach out to a therapist or helpline immediately, as therapists are trained to handle these stages of grief, and they can offer a safe, attentive presence to start building that space for you, even if it feels impossible right now.",
